{
  "id": "Compound::DB00220 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Nelfinavir is known to bind to Cyp2b6, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in drug metabolism. This binding leads to Cyp2b6 participating in various metabolic pathways, including oxidoreductase activity, steroid hydroxylase activity, and the Liver X Receptor Pathway. These pathways are all associated with the activity of Cyp3a4, a key enzyme in drug metabolism. The evidence suggests that Nelfinavir may influence Cyp3a4 through its interaction with Cyp2b6, potentially modulating its activity in metabolic processes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Nelfinavir could affect Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a consistent relationship, but further studies are needed to confirm the direct link between Nelfinavir and Cyp3a4.",
